  "state": "scoped-qualified",
  "acceptance": false,
  "complete_requirement_coverage": false,
  "scope": "Native C++/Python editing intent controller for complete RGB session histories. Selection synchronization replaces only the current draft membership and clears its whole-plane override; promoted masks remain frozen. Component switches promote nonidentity drafts; explicit promotion also supports same-component snapshots. Navigation freezes outgoing stages and starts a new identity visit over accumulated logical output. Reset changes only the current draft. Compatible camera/title/ROI/unrelated metadata refreshes retain historical intent. External pixels/storage/calibration or owner changes refuse adoption and require an explicit new editor. Every candidate is resolved and job-admitted before shared immutable state replacement; failed edits, limit readmission and external-navigation admission preserve the complete old capture. Editing/admission performs no pixel IO or callbacks. Preview commands retain all historical visits but omit final noncurrent-stack mapping; final Apply commands retain that policy and use existing session jobs/workflows. Immutable state copies and detached Python accessors preserve prior captures. All 378 actual ImageJ traces pass every selection/navigation/Reset/remap/whole-stack checkpoint through this controller, and all 5292 final stack reference rows pass including same-component promotion, active/noncurrent narrowing and masks. Recovery/late refusal, source guards, complete strict replay, worker publication and paired Undo/Redo pass. Four native suites and an installed public-header SDK consumer pass on Windows/Linux. Actual disposable installed Python interpreters run the new module and the existing session core/capture/workflow regression modules; all current cases pass. Preliminary native literal expectations used 255 instead of the ImageJ 256 mapping factor; the corrected literal test and raw variant are retained. Two Python fixture API mistakes (read-only calibration assignment, then shutdown on Application instead of its scheduler) are retained as failed runs. Final manifests differ from native qualification only in that Python test file. Main ImGui controls/preview/Auto/host Apply are intentionally still pending integration; this controller alone does not close the existing six-case editor probe or prove real widget acceptance. The next integration packet is specified in RGB_NAVIGATION.md without changing any original requirement. Estimates cover declared native work; caller copies, provider caches, frontend copies, publication/history staging and RSS remain external. Exact scratch is CRC/every-member-SHA archived before confined deletion; installs/probes/logs and useful caches remain. All original 99 requirement/status triples and the existing failing Auto source-evidence gate remain unchanged.",
